course: dictionary
lesson: 3410
title: Explosive: more than a bang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Explosive can be a noun or an adjective, so the words around it tell you which meaning you need. Look at the sentence first.
explain: As a noun, an explosive is a substance or device that can blow up. «Detection dogs are trained to sniff out things such as drugs, explosives, fruit carried in bags, money...» Dogs look for things that can blow up, so explosives must be things like that.
explain: As an adjective, explosive means able or likely to explode, or sudden and violent. «Humphry Davy made a safety lamp for coal miners» shows how dangerous explosive gas can be. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Explosive means able or likely to explode.
fact: An explosive (noun) is a substance or device that can blow up, such as dynamite or a bomb.
fact: Explosive can also mean sudden and violent, as in «an explosive temper», or very fast, as in explosive growth.
fact: «Highly explosive» means very likely to blow up, and such materials are handled only by adults or experts.
fact: «Explosive eruptions» happen when gas trapped in sticky magma bursts out; runny lava flows out more gently.
exercise: «Detection dogs are trained to sniff out things such as drugs, explosives, fruit carried in bags, money and even some illnesses.» What are explosives in this sentence? | Dogs that sniff out illnesses | Loud noises in the street | *Substances or devices that can blow up | Fruit and money
exercise: «Humphry Davy made a safety lamp for coal miners in 1815: a metal mesh around the flame stops it lighting explosive gas in the mine.» What does explosive gas mean? | Gas that makes people sleepy | Gas that is cold and clear | *Gas that can blow up | Gas that smells of flowers
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the calmer lava in «Gas trapped in sticky magma makes explosive eruptions; runny lava flows out more gently.» | explosive | sticky | *runny | trapped
test: «Before machines, tunnels were dug by hand with picks, shovels and explosives by the light of candles or lamps.» What are explosives here? | *Substances that can blow up, used to break rock | Metal pipes | Light bulbs | Tiny animals
test: Why was the safety lamp made, according to «a metal mesh around the flame stops it lighting explosive gas in the mine, and it saved many lives»? | *To stop the flame lighting explosive gas in the mine | To light the tunnels for the children | To stop the rain | To cook food for the miners
exam: Which word best describes a situation that is very tense and could suddenly turn into trouble? | Runny | Gentle | Sleepy | *Explosive
